## Source
2026-06-04 foundations audit + author decision: the audit prompt
becomes a standing pre-release QA process. AGENTS.md:61-67 already
establishes the pattern for posture properties that drift as the tool
changes (UX-PROCESS.md, SECURITY-PROCESS.md): agents do the legwork, a
falsifiable subset runs in CI, humans gate the findings, re-run per
release. Foundations coherence (do the docs and the guards still
match?) is exactly that class.

## Fix
Write FOUNDATIONS-PROCESS.md modeled on the two existing process docs:
- Sweep: inventory contracts across the constitution (AGENTS.md), the
  rationale (PEP), the spec, process docs, and the guard tests.
- Verify: compute the disjoint union (stated-without-guard) U
  (guarded-without-statement) -- the healthy region is the
  intersection; each side has a distinct remediation (a test vs a
  sentence). List tensions between doc sites explicitly.
- Communicate: check the canonical-source-plus-pointers structure;
  flag contracts living only in decision records (charter) or
  CHANGELOG.
Reference it from the AGENTS.md posture paragraph alongside UX and
security; add it to the pre-release checklist the release flow runs.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] FOUNDATIONS-PROCESS.md exists with the three-phase method
      (sweep / verify-disjoint-union / communicate)
- [ ] AGENTS.md posture paragraph references it
- [x] Release procedure lists it alongside UX and security audits
      (delivered: IDH release-skill PR #278, merged 2026-06-04 -- Agent C
      foundations coherence in the parallel audit panel)
- [ ] make check passes
